Rule 1 (inputs must have identical shapes for elementwise pairing)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 2 (both inputs must have numeric or boolean dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10)
>>
Rule 3 (empty arrays must have exactly matching shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) then (ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i))
>>
Rule 4 (boolean a must contain only 0/1 values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then (min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1)
>>
Rule 5 (boolean b must contain only 0/1 values)
{v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_2) = 0 then (min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_2) ≤ 1)
